  "body": "### Summary\nAs a user, I want the GIF picker's ✕ to have a 44 pt hit region, so that I do not miss it.\n\n### Scope\n- `App/SwiftHFR/Gif/GifPickerView.swift:131-137` uses the same bare `.plain` glyph button as the chip ✕ and the poll ⊖ that #1292 fixes for #1156.\n- Fix: `.minimumHitRegion()` (added by #1292) on the label, plus a hosted frame test as in `ComposerTouchTargetTests`.\n\n### Blocked by\n#1292\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] The ✕ hit region is at least 44×44 pt and its look is unchanged.\n- [ ] A hosted test fails before the fix.\n\nFound by the adversarial review of #1292 (Opus 5.5, r1292), finding 7.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_\n",
